> Aside from how they are organized, what are the difference between
> jbovlaste and vlasisku that are not immediately obvious?  For instance, is
> there any practical difference in their authority, their source material,
> or how they are compiled?
>

Yes, la vlasisku uses the same database as la jbovlaste but can lag behind
la jbovlaste due to non-immediate updates.
la jbovlaste is a live database reflecting opinions of particular people.
Anyone can edit definitions, vandalism is also theoretically possible.


